  "question": {
    "text": "<p>An optical arrangement consists of two concave mirrors <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>, and a convex lens <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math> with a common principal axis, as shown in the figure. The focal length of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. The radii of curvature of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>24</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>, respectively. The distance between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. A point object <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math> is placed at the mid-point between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> on the axis. When the distance between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mn>7</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>, one of the images coincides with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> is _____(Consider the case which gives minimum value).</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/f968ce8f-eb0b-46fb-9b42-78c719c2e1dd.png\" style=\"width: 500px; height: 214px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "80",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/7398febf-bd6f-43ff-b564-ff1d681910c1.png\" style=\"width: 600px; height: 313px;\" /></p><p>For reflection from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>:</p><p>Applying mirror formula, we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>v</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfenced></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></mfenced></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>v</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>12</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>&nbsp;(for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>)</p><p>For refraction from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math>:</p><p>Applying lens equation, we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>v</mi></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>u</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>f</mi></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>v</mi></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>80</mn></mrow></mfenced></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>80</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;(for&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>)</p><p>This image should be at focus of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mn>20</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>80</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mn>7</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>150</mn></math></p><p>Also,</p><p>If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is formed at pole of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math></p><p>then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mn>7</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>80</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>80</mn></math></p><p>And further if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is formed at centre of curvature of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;then</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mn>7</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>80</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>220</mn></math></p><p>So value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>&nbsp;can be either&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>80</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>or</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>150</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>or</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>220</mn></math>.</p></blockquote>",
